abstract: >-
  perinatal-ews scans public natality data and flags counties where maternal and
  newborn outcomes (preterm birth, low birth weight, late or no prenatal care,
  gestational hypertension) are worse than their own recent history and the
  all-county trend predict. It uses empirical-Bayes shrinkage, overdispersion
  modelling and false-discovery-rate control, runs the same test within
  subgroups, reports within-county equity gaps, and monitors its own data
  quality, distribution drift and detection performance. Version 0.3 adds
  county context (adult health, social factors, drug overdose deaths, opioid
  treatment capacity for pregnant and postpartum patients, and hospitals with
  labour and delivery care), a cross-validated machine-learning comparison with
  similar counties, and a need-versus-access review list. Version 0.4 adds an
  AI assistant that answers questions by calling the tool's data functions
  and checks every figure in its answers, and a state view. Version 0.5 adds
  county types from unsupervised clustering, a machine-learning (Isolation
  Forest) data-quality check, cross-conformal 90% prediction ranges for the
  similar-county comparison, and an interactive county map. Version 0.6 adds
  small-numbers analysis: state level, multi-year pooling that reports
  unavailable years, and combining of small racial and ethnic groups.
